#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:2
msgid "Marker: Sending Basic Shapes (C++)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:4
msgid ""
"**Goal:** Show how to use ``visualization_msgs/msg/Marker`` messages to send "
"basic shapes to RViz."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:6
msgid "**Tutorial level:** Intermediate"
msgstr "**教學等級：** 中級"

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:8
msgid "**Time:** 15 Minutes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:12
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:16
msgid ""
"This tutorial assumes you are already comfortable with writing ROS 2 C++ "
"nodes and building packages with ``colcon``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:19
msgid "Intro"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:20
msgid ""
"Unlike many other RViz displays, the ``Marker`` display lets you visualize "
"data without RViz needing to know the meaning of that data ahead of time. "
"Instead, your node sends primitive objects through ``visualization_msgs/msg/"
"Marker`` messages, and RViz renders them as arrows, boxes, spheres, "
"cylinders, and other marker types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:23
msgid ""
"This tutorial shows how to send the four basic shapes: cube, sphere, "
"cylinder, and arrow. We'll create a program that sends out a new marker "
"every second, replacing the last one with a different shape."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:26
msgid ""
"If you want a broader reference for marker fields and object types after "
"this walkthrough, see :doc:`Marker: Display types <../Marker-Display-types/"
"Marker-Display-types>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:29
msgid "Create a package"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:30
msgid ""
"Get the package from the `visualization_tutorials repository <https://github."
"com/ros-visualization/visualization_tutorials>`_ and build it in your "
"workspace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:32
#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:193
msgid "$ colcon build --packages-select visualization_marker_tutorials"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:37
msgid "Sending markers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:40
msgid "The code"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:41
msgid ""
"The code for this tutorial lives in the ``visualization_marker_tutorials`` "
"package. You can read it in `basic_shapes.cpp <https://github.com/ros-"
"visualization/visualization_tutorials/blob/ros2/"
"visualization_marker_tutorials/src/basic_shapes.cpp>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:45
msgid "The code explained"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:46
msgid ""
"Ok, let's break down the code piece by piece. We start by including the "
"headers used by the node, including ``rclcpp`` and the ``visualization_msgs/"
"msg/Marker`` message definition."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:49
msgid ""
"#include <memory>\n"
"\n"
"#include \"rclcpp/logging.hpp\"\n"
"#include \"rclcpp/rclcpp.hpp\"\n"
"#include \"visualization_msgs/msg/marker.hpp\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:57
msgid ""
"This should look familiar. We initialize ROS 2, create a node, and create a "
"publisher on the ``visualization_marker`` topic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:60
msgid ""
"rclcpp::init(argc, argv);\n"
"auto node = rclcpp::Node::make_shared(\"basic_shapes\");\n"
"auto marker_pub = node->create_publisher<visualization_msgs::msg::Marker>(\n"
"  \"visualization_marker\", 1);\n"
"rclcpp::Rate loop_rate(1);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:68
msgid ""
"You should have seen the ROS 2 include and node setup by now. The publisher "
"is what matters for RViz, because the ``Marker`` display subscribes to the "
"same topic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:71
msgid ""
"Here we create an integer to keep track of what shape we're going to "
"publish. The four types we'll be using here all use the ``visualization_msgs/"
"msg/Marker`` message in the same way, so we can simply switch out the shape "
"type to demonstrate the four different shapes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:74
msgid "uint32_t shape = visualization_msgs::msg::Marker::CUBE;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:78
msgid ""
"This begins the meat of the program. First we create a new "
"``visualization_msgs/msg/Marker`` and begin filling it out. The header sets "
"the frame ID and timestamp for the marker."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:82
msgid ""
"visualization_msgs::msg::Marker marker;\n"
"marker.header.frame_id = \"my_frame\";\n"
"marker.header.stamp = rclcpp::Clock().now();"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:88
msgid ""
"We set ``frame_id`` to ``my_frame`` as an example. In a running system, this "
"should be the frame relative to which you want the marker pose to be "
"interpreted. Because this tutorial does not publish transforms, RViz will "
"need to use the same fixed frame later."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:92
msgid ""
"The namespace and ID fields are used together to create a unique name for "
"the marker. If another message arrives with the same namespace and ID, the "
"new marker replaces the old one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:95
msgid ""
"marker.ns = \"basic_shapes\";\n"
"marker.id = 0;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:100
msgid ""
"This ``type`` field specifies the kind of marker we're sending. The "
"available types are listed in the ``visualization_msgs/msg/Marker`` message. "
"Here we set the type to the ``shape`` variable, which changes each time "
"through the loop."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:104
msgid "marker.type = shape;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:108
msgid ""
"The ``action`` field specifies what to do with the marker. The values used "
"in ROS 2 are ``ADD``, ``DELETE``, and ``DELETEALL``. ``ADD`` is something of "
"a misnomer, because it really means \"create or modify\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:112
msgid "marker.action = visualization_msgs::msg::Marker::ADD;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:116
msgid ""
"Here we set the pose of the marker. This is a full 6-DOF pose relative to "
"the frame and time specified in the header. Here we place it at the origin "
"and use the identity orientation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:120
msgid ""
"marker.pose.position.x = 0;\n"
"marker.pose.position.y = 0;\n"
"marker.pose.position.z = 0;\n"
"marker.pose.orientation.x = 0.0;\n"
"marker.pose.orientation.y = 0.0;\n"
"marker.pose.orientation.z = 0.0;\n"
"marker.pose.orientation.w = 1.0;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:130
msgid ""
"Now we specify the scale of the marker. For the basic shapes, a scale of "
"``1.0`` in all directions means one meter on a side."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:133
msgid ""
"marker.scale.x = 1.0;\n"
"marker.scale.y = 1.0;\n"
"marker.scale.z = 1.0;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:139
msgid ""
"The color is specified as RGBA values in the range ``[0, 1]``. Here we use "
"opaque green. The alpha channel is especially important because markers are "
"transparent by default if ``a`` is left at ``0``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:143
msgid ""
"marker.color.r = 0.0f;\n"
"marker.color.g = 1.0f;\n"
"marker.color.b = 0.0f;\n"
"marker.color.a = 1.0;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:150
msgid ""
"The ``lifetime`` field controls how long the marker should stick around "
"before being deleted automatically. A zero duration means it should never be "
"deleted automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:153
msgid "marker.lifetime = rclcpp::Duration::from_nanoseconds(0);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:157
msgid "Now we publish the marker message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:159
msgid "marker_pub->publish(marker);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:163
msgid ""
"This code lets us show all four shapes while just publishing one marker "
"message. Based on the current shape, we set what the next shape to publish "
"will be."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:166
msgid ""
"switch (shape) {\n"
"  case visualization_msgs::msg::Marker::CUBE:\n"
"    shape = visualization_msgs::msg::Marker::SPHERE;\n"
"    break;\n"
"  case visualization_msgs::msg::Marker::SPHERE:\n"
"    shape = visualization_msgs::msg::Marker::ARROW;\n"
"    break;\n"
"  case visualization_msgs::msg::Marker::ARROW:\n"
"    shape = visualization_msgs::msg::Marker::CYLINDER;\n"
"    break;\n"
"  case visualization_msgs::msg::Marker::CYLINDER:\n"
"    shape = visualization_msgs::msg::Marker::CUBE;\n"
"    break;\n"
"}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:183
msgid "Sleep for one second and loop back to the top."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:185
msgid "loop_rate.sleep();"
msgstr ""

