#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:207
msgid "Viewing the markers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:208
msgid ""
"Now that the node is publishing markers, start RViz so you can view them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:210
msgid ""
"$ source install/setup.bash\n"
"$ ros2 run rviz2 rviz2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:215
msgid ""
"If you have never used RViz before, start with the :doc:`RViz User Guide <../"
"RViz-User-Guide/RViz-User-Guide>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:217
msgid ""
"Because we do not have any transforms set up, the first thing to do is set "
"the ``Fixed Frame`` to the frame used in the marker message, ``my_frame``. "
"Then add a ``Marker`` display. Notice that the default topic, "
"``visualization_marker``, is the same one being published by the node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Intermediate/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes.rst:221
msgid ""
"You should now see a marker at the origin that changes shape every second."
msgstr ""

